    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/06/nike-pegasus-41-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length ReactX and higher 37/27 mm stack give a mildly soft, well-protected heel landing, while the forefoot still feels slightly firmer and more grounded.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate with only a slight bounce, and the shoe feels best at easy/long paces rather than snappy for faster uptempo running.",
        "Stability: Rearfoot guidance is improved by medial/lateral heel sidewalls plus a stiff heel counter that helps center the foot, while the forefoot remains moderately flexible rather than highly rigid.",
        "Durability: Outsole grip is strong, but rearfoot lugs showed early wear around 40 miles; overall durability is described as average, with foam structure holding up reasonably well."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/06/nike-pegasus-41-review-6-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: ReactX foam plus a 4 mm stack increase makes the Pegasus 41 softer than recent versions, improves impact protection, and reduces bottoming out, but the forefoot Air Zoom areas can feel firmer and uneven until break-in.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is described as lively and bouncy with solid energy return (Nike claims +13% vs older React), with enough pop for moderate uptempo work, though overall weight limits snappiness.",
        "Stability: Fit/hold is secure through heel, midfoot, and toe box with a well-structured heel collar and good lockdown, and the waffle outsole adds traction-based stability, but torsional rigidity and true lateral structure are not deeply detailed.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability is a standout, with a tough rubber waffle design showing virtually no wear after 50+ miles and expected longevity for road use and light-to-medium dry trail running."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/nike-pegasus-41-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: ReactX is perceived as softer and comfortable overall, but both reviewers report the forefoot feels thin/under-cushioned, with less impact protection up front than in the heel.",
        "Responsiveness: The shoe has some bounce from ReactX + Air Zoom and occasional mild propulsion, but the ride is generally described as lacking pop/snappiness, with forefoot Zoom not very noticeable.",
        "Stability: Lockdown is strong via the internal midfoot band/lacing and supportive mesh, and the ride feels sturdy and secure; no specific torsional rigidity or heel-counter weaknesses were called out.",
        "Durability: Durability is a strength, with substantial/near full outsole rubber coverage and tread noted for longevity and traction, though the rubber compound is described as waxy and less tacky than desired."
      ]
    }
